  "notes": "{揚|あ}げる specifically means to deep-fry — to cook food by submerging it in hot oil. The kanji {揚|あ} distinguishes this verb from the many other あげる verbs.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n- Pair: {揚|あ}がる (intransitive — food is fried, comes out of oil)\n- Pattern: Xを{揚|あ}げる\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{揚|あ}げている means \"is in the process of deep-frying.\"\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {油|あぶら}で{揚|あ}げる: to fry in oil\n- カラッと{揚|あ}げる: to fry until crispy\n- {素揚|すあ}げ: deep-frying without batter\n- {揚|あ}げたて: freshly fried\n\nFRIED FOODS:\n- {天|てん}ぷら: tempura (batter-fried)\n- {唐揚|からあ}げ: Japanese fried chicken\n- コロッケ: croquette\n- フライ: deep-fried breaded food (tonkatsu, etc.)\n\nOTHER あげる VERBS:\n- {上|あ}げる: to raise\n- {挙|あ}げる: to cite, to hold up\n- {掲|あ}げる: to display, to hoist",
